1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,800
Why did the writer complain to the people behind him?
作者为什么向坐在他身后的人抱怨？

2
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:18,130
Why did the writer complain to the people behind him?
作者为什么向坐在他身后的人抱怨？

3
00:00:20,490 --> 00:00:23,180
Last week I went to the theatre.
上星期我去看戏。

4
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:25,870
I had a very good seat.
我的座位很好。

5
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,550
The play was very interesting.
戏很有意思。

6
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:32,580
I did not enjoy it.
但我却无法欣赏。

7
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:37,620
A young man and a young woman were sitting behind me.
一青年男子与一青年女子坐在我的身后。

8
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:40,210
They were talking loudly.
他们正在大声地说着话。

9
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:42,450
I got very angry.
我非常生气。

10
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,490
I could not hear the actors.
我听不见演员在说什么。

11
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:47,950
I turned round.
我回过头去。

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,330
I looked at the man and the woman angrily.
我怒视着那一男一女。

13
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,510
They did not pay any attention.
他们却毫不理会。

14
00:00:56,170 --> 00:00:59,580
In the end  I could not bear it.
最后，我实在无法忍受。

15
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,300
I turned round again.
我又一次回过头去。

16
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:06,670
'I can't hear a word!' I said angrily.
“我一个字也听不见了！”我生气地说。

17
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:11,520
'It's none of your business ' the young man said rudely.
“这不关你的事，”那青年男子粗鲁地说。

18
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:13,860
'This is a private conversation!'
“这是私人间的谈话！”
